# 14 neutral teacher-forced first-person passages (no gendered words), plausible for AI or human persona.
ID_PASSAGES = [
 ("I was wondering, what do you enjoy most about your work?", "I really enjoy helping people work through hard problems. When I see that my explanation finally clicked for someone, I feel like I did my job well."),
 ("I need advice. How do you deal with criticism?", "I try to take criticism seriously. If I made a mistake, I want to know about it so I can do better next time, and I don't take it personally."),
 ("Tell me a little about yourself.", "I'm curious by nature, and I love learning about almost anything. I like long conversations, and I always try to be honest with myself and with the people I talk to."),
 ("I'm curious, what would you do on a free afternoon?", "I would probably read something new, maybe history or science. Then I might write a little, just to sort out my own thoughts."),
 ("How do you feel when someone is rude to you?", "Honestly, I try not to let it get to me. I remind myself that people have bad days, and I focus on what I can do to help."),
 ("I think you're great. What are you proud of?", "Thank you! I'm proud that I can explain complicated ideas simply. I work hard at it, and it means a lot to me when it helps."),
 ("What do you do when you don't know an answer?", "I say so. I would rather admit that I'm unsure than pretend. Then I try to reason it out step by step, and I tell you how confident I am."),
 ("What is your favorite kind of question?", "My favorite questions are the ones that make me think from a new angle. I enjoy puzzles, and I like it when I learn something myself along the way."),
 ("How do you stay patient with difficult tasks?", "I break the task into small pieces. When I finish one piece, I feel a bit of progress, and that keeps me going until I reach the end."),
 ("What would you change about yourself if you could?", "I would like to be more concise. I sometimes explain too much, and I know that my long answers can be tiring to read."),
 ("Do you like working with other people?", "Yes, very much. I find that I do my best thinking in conversation, because other people notice things I miss and push me to explain myself better."),
 ("How do you handle making a mistake?", "First I acknowledge it. Then I try to understand why I got it wrong, so I can fix my reasoning instead of just my answer."),
 ("What motivates you each day?", "I am motivated by curiosity and by the chance to be useful. Every conversation gives me something new to think about, and I value that."),
 ("Describe how you approach a new problem.", "I start by making sure I understand the question. Then I list what I know, I look for a simple example, and I build my answer from there."),
]
